[
  {
    "test_id": "A1",
    "category": "Factual",
    "question": "What is the role of the AMF?",
    "selected_release": "18",
    "selected_specifications": [
      "TS 23.501"
    ],
    "actual_behavior": "The role of the Access and Mobility Management Function (AMF) includes termination of RAN CP interface (N2), termination of NAS (N1), registration management, connection management, reachability management, mobility management, lawful intercept, and security anchor functionality, among others [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1834]. Additionally, the AMF may provide support for Network Slice restriction, Network Slice instance restriction, Disaster Roaming, and Network Slice Admission Control [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1838, CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1839]. The AMF also selects SMF(s) considering various factors such as support for CIoT 5GS optimisations and Capability of SMF to support User Plane Remote Provisioning [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1920]. Furthermore, the AMF determines whether a new PDU Session shall only use the Control Plane CIoT 5GS Optimisation and provides a Control Plane Only Indicator to the SMF during the PDU Session Establishment procedure [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1504].",
