  {
    "test_id": "A2",
    "category": "Factual",
    "question": "What is the role of the SMF?",
    "selected_release": "18",
    "selected_specifications": [
      "TS 23.501"
    ],
    "actual_behavior": "The role of the SMF includes several key functions, such as: \n- Providing N4 information to the I-SMF for traffic detection, enforcement, and monitoring in UPF(s) [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1747].\n- Receiving N4 notifications related to traffic usage reporting and aggregating usage reports towards PCF/CHF [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1747].\n- Deciding whether buffering timers or amount of downlink data are handled by the UPF or SMF [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_742].\n- Instructing the UPF to forward applicable user plane traffic to the SMF [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_687].\n- Supporting PFD management by providing PFD(s) to the UPF and caching PFD(s) [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_687].\n- Providing Ethernet Packet Filter Set and forwarding rule(s) to the UPF based on the Ethernet frame structure and UE MAC address(es) [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_524].\n- Supporting User Plane Remote Provisioning [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1921].\n- Selecting and reselecting the UPF by considering UPF deployment scenarios [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1921].\n- Supporting interactions towards the CHF for network resource usage [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_780].",
