  {
    "test_id": "A3",
    "category": "Factual",
    "question": "What is the role of the UPF?",
    "selected_release": "18",
    "selected_specifications": [
      "TS 23.501"
    ],
    "actual_behavior": "The UPF plays a crucial role in managing the user plane, including traffic routing [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_642], UE IP address management [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_642], and CN Tunnel Info management [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_663]. It also supports branching point functionality for traffic measurement, replication, and bit rate enforcement [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_441], as well as traffic detection [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_663]. The UPF can be selected and reselected by the SMF based on various deployment scenarios and capabilities [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1921] [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.501_18.0.0_1922].",
