  {
    "test_id": "C1",
    "category": "Procedural",
    "question": "Explain the 5G registration procedure.",
    "selected_release": "18",
    "selected_specifications": [
      "TS 23.502"
    ],
    "actual_behavior": "The 5G registration procedure is initiated by the UE using one of the following Registration types: Initial Registration to the 5GS, Mobility Registration Update, or others [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_83]. The procedure involves the UE sending a Registration Request message to the AMF, which then responds with a Registration Accept message indicating that the Registration Request has been accepted [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_161]. The Registration procedure is based on the Registration procedure specified in clause 4.2.2.2.2 [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_1275] and provides the required functionality to register or deregister a UE/user with the 5GS [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_82]. The AMF may include a new 5G-GUTI in the Registration Accept message, which the UE shall use for both registrations if it is already in RM-REGISTERED state via another access in the same PLMN [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_161].",
    "retrieved_sources": [
