  {
    "test_id": "C2",
    "category": "Procedural",
    "question": "What are the major steps in UE registration?",
    "selected_release": "18",
    "selected_specifications": [
      "TS 23.502"
    ],
    "actual_behavior": "The major steps in UE registration are as follows: \n1. The UE initiates the Registration procedure using one of the Registration types, such as Initial Registration or Mobility Registration Update [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_83]. \n2. The UE indicates that it is moving from EPC and provides the Registration type, a 5G-GUTI, and a native 5G-GUTI (if available) [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_1147]. \n3. The UE includes the UE Policy Container containing the list of PSIs, indication of UE support for ANDSP and OSId (if available) [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_1147]. \n4. The AMF decides if the Registration Request needs to be rerouted [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_123]. \n5. If NAS security context does not exist, the NAS security initiation is performed [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_123]. \n6. The UE includes the full Registration Request message (if no NAS security context exists) [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_123]. \n7. The UE and AMF complete the registration procedure, which may involve PDU session establishment [CHUNK_ID: TS_23.502_18.0.0_1360].",
    "retrieved_sources": [
      {
